 *
 * Software bit-banged (GPIO simulated) I2C master-write driver for the
 * GC2145 camera sensor, on GPIO42 (SCL) / GPIO43 (SDA).
 *
 * IMPORTANT CORRECTION (see this file's previous revision history and
 * hardware/bk7258_i2c1.h for the full account): this board's GC2145
 * camera I2C bus is NOT the BK7258's hardware I2C1 peripheral, despite
 * GPIO42/43 supporting an I2C1_SCL/I2C1_SDA hardware pinmux function
 * (GPIO_DEV_I2C1_SCL/GPIO_DEV_I2C1_SDA in bk_avdk_smp's gpio_map.h).
 * That hardware-I2C1 assumption was this driver's original (incorrect)
 * design: on real hardware, every write timed out waiting for the I2C1
 * peripheral's sm_int interrupt, even though sm_bus_cfg read back
 * exactly as configured -- consistent with "the peripheral's dedicated
 * state machine is talking to a bus GC2145 was never wired to respond
 * on this way."
 *
 * Cross-checked against the two OpenVela-external reference projects
 * that actually target this exact AIDK board (beken_genie and volc_rtc,
 * both under bk_solution_ai/projects/, both linking the same
 * AIDK_AI玩具开发板_原理图.pdf as their hardware reference) rather than
 * the generic dvp_example project (whose default GPIO0/1 wiring this
 * board does not use -- GPIO0/1 are UART1_TXD/RXD here, per the
 * schematic and usr_gpio_cfg.h's GPIO_DEFAULT_DEV_CONFIG):
 *
 *   - Both beken_genie and volc_rtc override the *software-simulated*
 *     I2C0 instance's GPIO Kconfig options (CONFIG_SIM_I2C0_SCL_GPIO=42,
 *     CONFIG_SIM_I2C0_SDA_GPIO=43) -- i.e. GPIO42/43 ARE the correct
 *     physical pins, but the intended access method is bk_avdk_smp's
 *     sim_i2c_driver.c software bit-bang (CONFIG_DVP_CAMERA_I2C_ID=2,
 *     which ap/middleware/driver/i2c/i2c_unified.c routes to "GPIO
 *     simulated I2C (starting from I2C_ID_2)", i.e. NOT any hardware
 *     I2C unit), not the hardware I2C1 register block this driver
 *     originally used.
 *   - Both projects' usr_gpio_cfg.h leave GPIO42/43's *static* default
 *     function as GPIO_DEV_LCD_G2/GPIO_DEV_LCD_B7 (an RGB LCD data-line
 *     use this board does not actually populate), confirming the pins
 *     are NOT meant to be pinmux-selected to their I2C1_SCL/I2C1_SDA
